/* ============================================================================
   THE COMMISSION CARD: the King's commission in the upper right of the board (#421).
   Built by CommissionCardView over the match, and fed by the server alone.

   Every number is in the 1080-tall authored panel (theme.uss), copied from the
   approved mockup docs/dev-docs/design/art/king-of-the-week-commission-card.html.
   USS has no gradients or box shadows, so the card's 160deg brown gradient is its
   midpoint colour and the drop shadow is gone.

   TWO FORMS, CHOSEN BY SCREEN ASPECT IN CODE:
     above 2:1   the full card, 280 x 424, 24 from the top edge;
     2:1 or less the chip: image and number in the band above the table, which a
                 tap opens into the full card over the opponent's hero ring.

   THE CHIP'S BAND. Projected through RoyalCouncilCamera.Fit (the live board's
   camera; board_camera_fit.py models the retired BoardCameraRig), the opponent's
   Hero Power is the highest thing on the right of the table: its top sits near
   y 118 at 1920 x 1080 and y 199 at 1440 x 1080. The chip ends at y 112. An
   estimate from the prefab's mount points, so measure it.

   THE RIGHT INSET IS .emb-edge's ALONE (controller ruling, 2026-11-02): both the card and
   the chip carry it in the UXML and anchor at right 0, which audit_edge_safety.py requires.
   IT DOES NOT CLEAR THE PIXEL 5a's PUNCH-HOLE. That cutout is 136 px deep at this panel's
   1:1 scale and --edge-safe is 52, so the camera still covers about the right 30 px of the
   image (x 2264..2294, y 40..145). A known trade-off: moving further in puts the card on
   the opponent's Hero Power. The cutout depth is tracked in #350.

   THE TEXT IS MEASURED IN ONE FONT. The card sets Modern Antiqua, the font every button
   uses, so its widths can be checked against the .ttf rather than Unity's default theme
   font. The task 7 report has the arithmetic.
   ============================================================================ */

.cc-root {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
}

/* Catches the tap that closes an opened card anywhere on screen. Clear, and shown only while
   the chip's card is open, when board input is gated off anyway. */
.cc-scrim {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    display: none;
}

/* ---------- The full card ---------- */

.cc-card {
    position: absolute;
    top: 24px;
    right: 0;
    width: 280px;
    height: 424px;
    padding: 12px;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
    background-color: rgb(83, 56, 25);
    border-width: 4px;
    border-color: rgb(199, 154, 62);
    border-radius: 16px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/Art/Fonts/ModernAntiqua-Regular UITK.asset");
}

.cc-card__image {
    width: 172px;
    height: 172px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    align-self: center;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}

/* ONE LINE, AT 26 NOT THE MOCKUP's 32. The ribbon is 260 wide (the card's 248 of content plus
   its -6 margins). The longest name, "Return to Sender", is 305.7 px in bold at 32; 26 is the
   largest even size that fits, at 248.3. One size for all nine, because a per-name size would need
   runtime text measurement, which nothing in this repo does yet. The ellipsis is only a guard. A
   Label has no children, so overflow: hidden here cannot eat any. */
.cc-card__ribbon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin: -14px -6px 0 -6px;
    padding: 4px 0;
    background-color: rgb(124, 21, 16);
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: rgb(246, 231, 193);
    font-size: 26px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

/* Exactly the height the card leaves: a basis of 0 that grows and never shrinks. So the clip
   never takes a whole child the way a shrinkable overflow: hidden does; it only trims a line that
   would otherwise cross the card's bottom border. */
.cc-card__text {
    flex-basis: 0;
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-top: 8px;
    padding: 10px;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: rgb(236, 220, 180);
    border-radius: 6px;
}

/* Every label in the card: none of Label's default margin or padding, which the box's
   tight vertical budget cannot spare. */
.cc-card__line {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: rgb(56, 34, 15);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: normal;
}

.cc-card__rules {
    font-size: 28px;
}

/* A fixed height of one em keeps the mockup's line-height: 1. UI Toolkit has no
   line-height, and a 92px line would leave the box too little room for the line under it. */
.cc-card__score {
    height: 92px;
    font-size: 92px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: rgb(140, 28, 19);
}

.cc-card__sub {
    margin-top: 4px;
    font-size: 27px;
}

/* ---------- The chip (2:1 and narrower) ---------- */

.cc-chip {
    position: absolute;
    top: 8px;
    right: 0;
    height: 104px;
    padding: 8px;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    background-color: rgb(83, 56, 25);
    border-width: 4px;
    border-color: rgb(199, 154, 62);
    border-radius: 16px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/Art/Fonts/ModernAntiqua-Regular UITK.asset");
    display: none;
}

.cc-chip__image {
    width: 80px;
    height: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}

.cc-chip__score {
    min-width: 56px;
    height: 64px;
    margin: 0 0 0 8px;
    padding: 0 8px;
    background-color: rgb(236, 220, 180);
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 48px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: rgb(140, 28, 19);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: nowrap;
}

/* Greyed while the score needs a win: #8a6a3a, the approved colour. */
.cc-card__score.cc-score--if-win,
.cc-chip__score.cc-score--if-win {
    color: rgb(138, 106, 58);
}
